EXT. BRIDGE OF BONES, MISTY GORGE - DAWN

A narrow span of lashed ribs and vertebrae across a chasm. Fog boils below. Ravens circle.

SIR GARRICK WYNDHAM-ADEYEMI (40s, dented plate armor, a notched longsword) steps onto the bridge. Behind him, HEDDA STORMCALLER-BRAND (30s, furs, a bow across her back) and the boy TOBIN "TICK" FENWICK (14, oversized helmet, a lantern) wait at the edge.

GARRICK
Stay close.

HEDDA
I always do.

TICK
It creaks.

GARRICK
It's meant to.

They step out, single file. Ribs groan. A raven lands on a post and croaks. Hedda draws an arrow. Tick clutches the lantern.

From beneath the bridge, a long, wet rattle. Everything stops.

The span lurches. Ribs snap loose and tumble into the fog. Garrick seizes Tick by the collar while Hedda throws her bow across the gap, hooks a post, and hauls herself and the boy forward by the string. Tick screams, drops the lantern, and scoops it back up. Garrick hacks at a lashing that has caught his boot, and the bridge sags behind them.

They freeze, panting. The bridge rocks once, then settles.

TICK
Is it dead?

HEDDA
It was already dead.

GARRICK
It's gone. Move.

They run across, boots thundering on bone, and leap the final gap to solid ground. All three collapse, laughing and gasping.
